---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL, UPSTREAM_REPOSITORY_URL } from "../lib/site";

const previewChecks = [
  { label: "mandate scope · market & side", detail: "within mission" },
  { label: "leverage ≤ mission cap", detail: "20x ≤ 20x" },
  { label: "gross notional within budget", detail: "reservation ledger" },
  { label: "exchange minimums & tick size", detail: "size, price band" },
  { label: "BBO freshness & slippage bound", detail: "priced off live book" },
  { label: "stop-loss attached, reduce-only", detail: "mandatory" },
];

const controls = ["Pause", "Cancel entries", "Reduce 50%", "Close", "Revoke"];
---

<Layout>
  <!-- ── Hero ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-grid" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <div class="container hero-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow hero-eyebrow">Agentic Trading Environment · alpha · Hyperliquid testnet</p>

      <h1 class="hero-title display">
        Give an agent a market,<br />a budget, and a deadline.
      </h1>

      <p class="hero-sub">
        T3 Trade is an <strong>ATE — an Agentic Trading Environment</strong>. The coding
        agents you already run get a second thing to point at: a live Hyperliquid testnet
        account, reached through a typed, gated tool surface. The agent reads the market,
        plans, and explains itself. The environment enforces the rules.
      </p>

      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a id="download-btn" href="/download" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">
          <svg class="dl-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 814 1000" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="currentColor" d="M788.1 340.9c-5.8 4.5-108.2 62.2-108.2 190.5 0 148.4 130.3 200.9 134.2 202.2-.6 3.2-20.7 71.9-68.7 141.9-42.8 61.6-87.5 123.1-155.5 123.1s-85.5-39.5-164-39.5c-76.5 0-103.7 40.8-165.9 40.8s-105.6-57-155.5-127C46.7 790.7 0 663 0 541.8c0-194.4 126.4-297.5 250.8-297.5 66.1 0 121.2 43.4 162.7 43.4 39.5 0 101.1-46 176.3-46 28.5 0 130.9 2.6 198.3 99.2zm-234-181.5c31.1-36.9 53.1-88.1 53.1-139.3 0-7.1-.6-14.3-1.9-20.1-50.6 1.9-110.8 33.7-147.1 75.8-28.5 32.4-55.1 83.6-55.1 135.5 0 7.8 1.3 15.6 1.9 18.1 3.2.6 8.4 1.3 13.6 1.3 45.4 0 102.5-30.4 135.5-71.3z"/></svg>
          <span>Download for macOS</span>
        </a>
        <a class="hero-source-link" href={GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          <span>Run from source</span>
          <svg class="hero-source-arrow" width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M7 17L17 7M8 7h9v9"/></svg>
        </a>
        <p class="hero-caution">
          Alpha software. Places real orders on Hyperliquid <strong>testnet</strong> —
          there is no mainnet mode.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-preview">
        <figure class="hero-screenshot-frame">
          <img
            src="/t3trade-screenshot.webp"
            alt="T3 Trade running a BTC momentum mission: the agent's published plan, armed watches, and a live position card with entry, stop, and target"
            width="2400"
            height="1520"
            loading="eager"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </figure>
        <figcaption class="hero-preview-caption">
          A live mission: the agent publishes its plan and belief, arms watches at its stop
          and target, and the position card tracks entry, stop, and liquidation against the
          exchange.
        </figcaption>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Mission anatomy ──────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section id="missions" class="sec-missions">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>A mission is a mandate, not a chat.</h2>
        <p>
          One agent thread, one market, a written strategy, a maximum-loss budget, and an
          expiry. Everything the agent can do flows from that mandate — nothing outside it
          is reachable.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mission-grid">
        <div class="tile mission-tile">
          <div class="mission-tile-label">Wakes on events, not timers</div>
          <p>
            The agent registers watches — a price cross, an unrealised-PnL level, a candle
            close — and sleeps until one fires. It wakes to a fresh snapshot of the account,
            position, resting orders, and remaining budget.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="tile mission-tile">
          <div class="mission-tile-label">The exchange is the authority</div>
          <p>
            Positions, orders, and fills are always read back from Hyperliquid. The database
            records what T3 Trade <em>did</em>; the exchange remains the source of what is
            <em>true</em>.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="tile mission-tile">
          <div class="mission-tile-label">Budgets are enforced, not suggested</div>
          <p>
            Loss accounting is pure, property-tested contract code. An exhausted budget blocks
            new exposure while keeping the stops that protect what's already open.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Preview checklist (signature) ────────────────────────── -->
  <section id="rails" class="sec-checklist">
    <div class="container checklist-inner">
      <div class="checklist-copy">
        <div class="section-head" style="margin-bottom:0">
          <h2>Every order earns its way to the signer.</h2>
          <p>
            Before anything is signed, a 17-item deterministic preview runs: mandate,
            leverage, notional, exchange minimums, the reservation ledger, and a mandatory
            stop-loss. A failed check is a rejected order — the agent cannot talk its way
            past it.
          </p>
          <ul class="rail-list">
            <li>
              <strong>No position stays unprotected.</strong> Every acknowledged increase must
              have a confirmed exchange-native reduce-only stop resting against it, reconciled
              against the canonical position size.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Submission is idempotent.</strong> A deterministic client order id plus a
              local idempotency key means a retried request returns the existing record instead
              of a second order.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Controls never need the agent.</strong> Pause, cancel entries, reduce,
              close, and revoke run deterministically even with the agent's provider process
              stopped.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="checklist-visual">
        <div class="tile preview-card">
          <div class="preview-head">
            <span class="preview-title">trading_preview_order</span>
            <span class="preview-status">17 checks</span>
          </div>
          <ul class="preview-list">
            {previewChecks.map((check) => (
              <li>
                <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
                <span class="preview-check-label">{check.label}</span>
                <span class="preview-check-detail">{check.detail}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
            <li class="preview-more">… then, and only then, sign &amp; submit</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="controls-strip" aria-label="Deterministic mission controls">
          <span class="controls-strip-label">Runs without the agent:</span>
          {controls.map((control) => (
            <span class="control-chip">{control}</span>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Harnesses ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section id="harnesses" class="sec-harness">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>The agents you already run.</h2>
        <p>
          T3 Trade drives the coding-agent CLIs installed on your machine, with the
          subscriptions you already pay for. The agent plans and explains; only the harness
          ever touches the signer key.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="harness-grid">
        <div class="harness">
          <div class="harness-mark"><img src="/harnesses/claude-ai-icon.svg" alt="" /></div>
          <div class="harness-meta">
            <div class="harness-name">Claude Code</div>
            <div class="harness-tag">claude auth login</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="harness">
          <div class="harness-mark"><img src="/harnesses/openai_dark.svg" alt="" /></div>
          <div class="harness-meta">
            <div class="harness-name">Codex CLI</div>
            <div class="harness-tag">codex login</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="harness">
          <div class="harness-mark"><img src="/harnesses/opencode-dark.svg" alt="" /></div>
          <div class="harness-meta">
            <div class="harness-name">OpenCode</div>
            <div class="harness-tag">opencode auth</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="harness">
          <div class="harness-mark"><img src="/harnesses/cursor_light.svg" alt="" /></div>
          <div class="harness-meta">
            <div class="harness-name">Cursor</div>
            <div class="harness-tag">cursor-agent</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="harness">
          <div class="harness-mark"><img src="/harnesses/grok-dark.svg" alt="" /></div>
          <div class="harness-meta">
            <div class="harness-name">Grok CLI</div>
            <div class="harness-tag">grok login</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Arming / signer key ──────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section id="arming" class="sec-arming">
    <div class="container arming-inner">
      <div class="tile arming-card">
        <div class="arming-row">
          <span class="arming-state arming-state--safe">
            <span class="arming-dot"></span> No signer key
          </span>
          <span class="arming-desc">
            Read-only. Missions, watches, and plans — nothing is signed or submitted.
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="arming-divider" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="arming-row">
          <span class="arming-state arming-state--armed">
            <span class="arming-dot"></span> Key present
          </span>
          <span class="arming-desc">
            Live execution on testnet. There is no second flag.
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="arming-copy">
        <div class="section-head" style="margin-bottom:0">
          <h2>Armed only when you arm it.</h2>
          <p>
            Hyperliquid is a signed-order exchange, so live execution needs a key. T3 Trade
            doesn't have wallet onboarding yet — for now you provision a single
            <strong>interim signer key</strong> in one canonical location
            (<code>~/.t3trade/secrets</code>), and its presence is the arming switch.
            Without it, the whole environment runs read-only. The key never appears in
            logs, reports, or the database. Deliberately blunt for the alpha; proper key
            management is future work.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Current state ────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section id="state" class="sec-state">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>What it is, and what it isn't.</h2>
        <p>The interesting claims are about containment, not alpha.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="state-grid">
        <div class="tile state-card">
          <div class="state-card-label state-card-label--is">Today</div>
          <ul>
            <li>Scoped, budgeted perp-futures missions on Hyperliquid testnet</li>
            <li>Deterministic order preview, mandatory stops, idempotent submission</li>
            <li>Operator controls that work with the agent stopped</li>
            <li>Web app + macOS (Apple Silicon) desktop build; other platforms from source</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="tile state-card">
          <div class="state-card-label state-card-label--isnt">Not today</div>
          <ul>
            <li>No mainnet mode — testnet only, by design</li>
            <li>No strategy library, no signals, no promised returns</li>
            <li>No wallet onboarding — one interim signer key you provision yourself</li>
            <li>No unattended operation against real funds, and no mobile app</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Open source ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section id="open" class="sec-open">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head" style="margin-bottom:0">
        <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:14px">Open source</div>
        <h2>A fork with a paper trail.</h2>
        <p>
          T3 Trade is an MIT-licensed fork of
          <a class="inline-link" href={UPSTREAM_REPOSITORY_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">T3 Code</a>
          by Ping Labs. The trading surface lives in a handful of clearly-bounded packages;
          everything else stays close to upstream, and every intentional divergence is
          recorded in a patch ledger.
        </p>
        <div class="open-actions">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href={GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Browse the source
          </a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={`${GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL}/blob/main/docs/architecture/trading-execution.md`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Read the execution design
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── Final CTA ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section id="download" class="sec-cta">
    <div class="container cta-inner">
      <h2 class="display cta-title">Run a mission on testnet.</h2>
      <p class="cta-sub">
        Download the alpha, fund a testnet account, write a mandate, and watch the
        harness hold the line.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a id="cta-download-btn" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/download">
          Download for macOS
        </a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href={GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Run from source</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  section {
    position: relative;
    padding: 96px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .section-head {
    margin-bottom: 56px;
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .section-head h2 {
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    line-height: 1.05;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }

  .section-head p {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: 18px;
    max-width: 620px;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  }

  .section-head p strong {
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .section-head code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85em;
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .inline-link {
    color: var(--fg);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: rgba(250, 250, 250, 0.35);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .inline-link:hover {
    text-decoration-color: var(--fg);
  }

  /* ── Hero ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .hero {
    padding: 72px 0 60px;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-top: 0;
  }

  .hero-grid {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    background-image:
      linear-gradient(to right, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.035) 1px, transparent 1px),
      linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.035) 1px, transparent 1px);
    background-size: 48px 48px;
    mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse 80% 60% at 50% 40%, black 40%, transparent 100%);
    -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse 80% 60% at 50% 40%, black 40%, transparent 100%);
  }

  .hero-inner {
    position: relative;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .hero-eyebrow {
    margin-top: 40px;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .hero-title {
    font-size: clamp(38px, 5.4vw, 72px);
    margin: 20px auto 22px;
    max-width: 22ch;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .hero-sub {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: clamp(16px, 1.4vw, 19px);
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto 36px;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .hero-sub strong {
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 56px;
  }

  .dl-icon {
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .hero-source-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    transition: color 0.18s ease;
  }

  .hero-source-link:hover {
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  .hero-source-arrow {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    opacity: 0.6;
    transition: transform 0.18s ease, opacity 0.18s ease;
  }

  .hero-source-link:hover .hero-source-arrow {
    transform: translate(2px, -2px);
    opacity: 1;
  }

  .hero-caution {
    color: var(--fg-dim);
    font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    max-width: 460px;
  }

  .hero-caution strong {
    color: var(--warn);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .hero-preview {
    max-width: 1180px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    transform: perspective(2000px) rotateX(2deg);
    transition: transform 0.6s ease;
  }

  .hero-preview:hover {
    transform: perspective(2000px) rotateX(0deg);
  }

  .hero-screenshot-frame {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    aspect-ratio: 2400 / 1520;
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: #0a0a0c;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    box-shadow: 0 28px 64px -28px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.75);
  }

  .hero-screenshot-frame img {
    width: calc(100% + 4px);
    height: calc(100% + 4px);
    margin: -2px;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center top;
  }

  .hero-preview-caption {
    margin-top: 16px;
    color: var(--fg-dim);
    font-size: 13px;
    max-width: 640px;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
  }

  /* ── Missions ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .mission-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .mission-tile {
    padding: 26px 24px;
  }

  .mission-tile-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .mission-tile p {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .mission-tile em {
    color: var(--fg);
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  /* ── Checklist (signature) ────────────────────────────────── */
  .sec-checklist {
    background: #09090b;
  }

  .checklist-inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.05fr;
    gap: 64px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .rail-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
    margin-top: 28px;
  }

  .rail-list li {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    padding-left: 18px;
    border-left: 2px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 35%, transparent);
  }

  .rail-list strong {
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .preview-card {
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .preview-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .preview-title {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  .preview-status {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    color: var(--accent);
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border: 1px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 999px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .preview-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .preview-list li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    padding: 9px 0;
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--border);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
  }

  .preview-list li svg {
    color: var(--ok);
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .preview-check-label {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .preview-check-detail {
    color: var(--fg-faint);
    font-size: 11px;
  }

  .preview-more {
    color: var(--fg-dim);
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .controls-strip {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-top: 16px;
  }

  .controls-strip-label {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--fg-dim);
    margin-right: 4px;
  }

  .control-chip {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    padding: 4px 10px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02);
  }

  /* ── Harnesses ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .sec-harness {
    background: #09090b;
  }

  .harness-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, 1fr);
    gap: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .harness {
    padding: 22px 20px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 14px;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.015), transparent);
    transition: background 0.2s ease;
  }

  .harness:last-child {
    border-right: 0;
  }

  .harness:hover {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.025);
  }

  .harness-mark {
    color: var(--fg);
    opacity: 0.95;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
  }

  .harness-mark img {
    width: 22px;
    height: 22px;
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  .harness-meta {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .harness-name {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-bottom: 2px;
  }

  .harness-tag {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--fg-dim);
  }

  /* ── Arming ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .arming-inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.1fr;
